  "result": "Perfect! All 181 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support:\n\n**src/dates.js** - Added utility function:\n- **getLastDayOfMonth(dateStr)** - Returns the last day of the month for a given date\n  - Correctly handles all months\n  - Accounts for leap years (Feb 29 in leap years, Feb 28 otherwise)\n  - Returns date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n\n**src/invoices.js** - Updated createInvoice:\n- Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Supports three payment terms:\n  - `'NET14'`: due 14 days after issue date\n  - `'NET30'`: due 30 days after issue date (default)\n  - `'EOM'`: due on the last day of the issue date's month\n- Returns TERMS_INVALID for unknown terms\n- Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on the returned invoice\n\n**src/errors.js** - Added error code:\n- `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM.\"\n\n**Tests** - 15 new tests covering:\n- Default NET30 terms calculation\n- NET14 and NET30 explicit terms\n- EOM terms (month-end invoices)\n- EOM edge cases (February leap and non-leap years, month boundaries)\n- Invalid and unknown terms rejection\n- getLastDayOfMonth for all months and leap years\n\nThe implementation correctly handles all edge cases including leap years and month boundaries, with all date arithmetic performed in UTC.",
